//api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't have a strong opinion on `PascalCase` vs `snake_case` for namespaces.\r\nI _do_ have an opinion on consistency, which is that it's good. Better to have one standard (and possibly change it in the future), than to have none at all.\r\n\r\nOne argument brought up in the core meeting for `PascalCase` was that it makes names for things like `Math` or `Memory` more consistent, both of which are currently `class` instead of `namespace` even though they are not supposed to be instantiated (changing soon for `Math`). \r\nBut IIRC there weren't any super strong opinions there either.\r\n\r\nI skimmed the code, seems fine to me. It would have been nice to mention there is one opinionated change among the renames (`godot::details` to `GodotTypeInfo::Internal`), but that change is fine by me.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#pullrequestreview-2708534423","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104043","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#pullrequestreview-2708534423"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104043"}},"submitted_at":"2025-03-23T11:06:59Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2709060802,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6hePzC","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ